      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. but honestly, it feels like a lot of these \"character\" arguments are just excuses to keep people out or keep housing prices high. is it even worth engaging with them deeply, or is it better to just frame their concerns as outdated NIMBYism so the group understands this is just how modern cities have to evolve?",
